NAME = Monomer_r2SCAN3c_CPCM.inp
|  1> # N-Methyl-2-pyrrolidone (NMP): gas-phase-guess Opt + Freq with CPCM solvation
|  2> #
|  3> # NOTE ON SOLVENT NAME: unlike ethanol/acetone/DMF/benzene/etc., NMP does not
|  4> # appear with confidence in ORCA's built-in named SMD solvent list (could not
|  5> # verify "nmp" / "n-methylpyrrolidone" / "n-methyl-2-pyrrolidone" as a
|  6> # recognized keyword). To avoid a repeat of the earlier DMF/XTB2 keyword
|  7> # error, this uses plain CPCM with an EXPLICITLY specified dielectric
|  8> # constant and refractive index instead of relying on a named-solvent
|  9> # keyword - this syntax is guaranteed valid regardless of whether NMP is in
| 10> # ORCA's named list.
| 11> #   epsilon (dielectric constant) = 32.2
| 12> #   refrac  (refractive index)    = 1.468
| 13> # (both are standard literature values for NMP at ~20-25 C)
| 14> # This does NOT include the SMD-specific non-electrostatic (CDS) term with
| 15> # NMP-specific surface-tension/H-bonding parameters - only the CPCM
| 16> # electrostatic (dielectric) contribution. If the full SMD CDS term is
| 17> # needed for NMP specifically, that requires additional solvent descriptors
| 18> # (Abraham's alpha/beta, macroscopic surface tension, aromatic/halogen
| 19> # fractions) that would need to be looked up and entered via a %smd block.
| 20> #
| 21> # Starting geometry: idealized regular-pentagon-based guess for the
| 22> # pyrrolidone ring (N-C(=O)-CH2-CH2-CH2-, closing back to N) plus the
| 23> # N-methyl group; bond lengths/angles are only approximate and will relax
| 24> # substantially during optimization.
| 25> 
| 26> ! r2SCAN-3c TightSCF Opt Freq KeepDens CPCM
| 27> 
| 28> %cpcm
| 29>   epsilon 32.2
| 30>   refrac  1.468
| 31> end
| 32> 
| 33> * xyz 0 1
| 34> N     0.000000    1.276000    0.000000
| 35> C    -1.213000    0.394000    0.000000
| 36> C    -0.750000   -1.032000    0.000000
